# Environment variables

Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in. Never commit a real `.env.local`.

The public menu is bundled with the app. Staff access and order submission use
Supabase in production; fill in the required values below before deployment.

## Database

# Managed Postgres (Supabase, Neon, RDS). Use the pooled connection string
# for the app and the direct one for migrations.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"
DIRECT_URL="postgresql://user:password@host:5432/postgres?sslmode=require"

# Supabase only. The service role key never reaches the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://your-project.supabase.co"
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="your-anon-key"
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="your-service-role-key"

## Authentication

# The admin and kitchen routes must sit behind a real session before launch.
# The prototype does not authenticate anybody.
AUTH_SECRET="a-long-random-string"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"

## Payments

# Chosen and onboarded by the restaurant, not by the developer. No payment
# provider is wired up in this prototype and no card details are collected.
# Keep the secret key on the server only.
PAYMENT_PROVIDER=""
PAYMENT_SECRET_KEY=""
PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

## Rate limiting and abuse protection

# Upstash Redis or equivalent, for the public order endpoint.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=""
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=""

## Object storage (approved food and shop photographs)

# Private bucket. The site serves signed or CDN URLs, never the bucket.
S3_BUCKET="chickadys-media"
S3_REGION="ap-south-1"
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_MEDIA_CDN_BASE=""

## Monitoring

SENTRY_DSN=""
DATADOG_SITE=""
DATADOG_API_KEY=""

## Rate limits (requests per window, per IP)

RATE_LIMIT_ORDERS_PER_MINUTE="5"
RATE_LIMIT_RESERVATIONS_PER_HOUR="3"
